## 2. Real HTTP verification on the production build
Run `npm run build` then `npm run start` (or the standalone server). Against that server, not the dev server:
1. Leak test: create one hidden item of each searchable and sitemap type (draft, archived, unpublished, pending, retracted-without-page if any, private manuscript, reviewer data, alumni). Prove none appears in /search results, /sitemap.xml, the RSS feeds or the ICS feed. Remove the fixtures after.
2. /search: empty query, 1 character, very long query, quote and operator characters, SQL metacharacters, unicode, and a 31st request in a minute (429). Show status codes.
3. Headers on key pages: noindex on /search, canonical URLs correct and absolute, robots.txt content, sitemap URL count per type.
4. Fix the "stale RSC payload on first request after publish" issue: check that publish, correct, retract, news and event changes call the right revalidatePath and revalidateTag. Prove it with a before and after request.

## 3. Accessibility
1. Install `@axe-core/playwright` and `@playwright/test` as devDependencies. Add `npm run test:e2e`.
2. Run axe against these routes at desktop and 375px width: /, /search, /lecturers, one lecturer page, /journal, one article, /journal/submit (signed in as an author), /alumni, /alumni/submit, /events, /news, /courses, /handbook, /downloads, /contact, /login, and the admin dashboard. Zero serious or critical violations. Fix real issues; do not disable rules. List any minor ones left with a reason.
3. Manual checks by keyboard in the browser, reported route by route: skip link, visible focus on every control, tab order, the Tiptap editor reachable and escapable, the search box, dialogs trap and restore focus, forms announce errors.
4. Colour contrast on the theme tokens (text on background, muted text, buttons, links in prose). Report ratios.
5. Every image has alt text or is marked decorative. Lecturer photos use the lecturer's name. The journal PDF links state the file type and size.

